            <ArticleTitle>IBD sharing around the PPARG locus is not increased in dizygotic twins or their mothers.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>315</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Busjahn et al reported finding linkage between PPARG (3p25) and being a dizygotic (DZ) twin. We differentiate, as do the authors, between the conception of DZ twins, and being the viable result of such a conception.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
